' Cross-deploy funding by the installer of a signed continuation (DR-68, decision D5).
' Under P1 uniform signing and Rule 4, an installer's unsigned trigger carries the
' installer's region. A later deploy that fires the trigger pays only its own
' work; the COMM in the installer's region draws on the installer's located purse,
' authorized by the stored signed term and bounded by the purse balance at R0.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-68);
'                  publications/cost-accounting/cost-accounted-rho.tex
'                  (sec:rewrites Rules 1-5, def:sugar-uniform, def:funding-proof).
' Palette:  clients = supply blue · runtime = process lilac · funding = gate teal
'           installer purse = pool green · gateway purse = capability indigo
'           debit = red arrows · authorization = blue arrows
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/installer-funded-continuation-sequence.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh installer-funded-continuation-sequence.puml)

@startuml installer-funded-continuation-sequence
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $ca_neutral
  LifeLineBorderColor #666666
  ParticipantBorderColor #333333
  BoxBorderColor #999999
}
title Installer-signed continuation funded by the installer's purse (DR-68)

actor "Installer" as Installer $ca_supply
actor "Gateway client" as Gateway $ca_supply
participant "Proposer and\nvalidators" as Node $ca_gate
participant "Reducer and\nnative meter" as Reducer $ca_process
participant "Funding family\nselection" as Family $ca_gate
participant "Installer\nlocated purse" as InstallerPurse $ca_pool
participant "Gateway\nsigned sources" as GatewayPurse $ca_capability

== Installation (earlier block) ==
Installer -> Node : offered deploy signed by the installer
Node -> Reducer : execute the installer's term
Reducer -> Reducer : store trigger continuation\nwith the installer's region (stored signed term)

== Trigger (later block) ==
Gateway -> Node : offered deploy signed by the gateway
Node -> Reducer : execute the gateway's term
Reducer -> Reducer : send matches the stored trigger
Reducer -> Family : obligations of this candidate\n(COMM in the installer region,\nbody work in the gateway region)
Family -[$ca_instantiate]-> InstallerPurse : eligible for installer-region obligations\nauthorized by the stored signed term
Family -[$ca_instantiate]-> GatewayPurse : eligible for gateway-region obligations\nauthorized by the gateway envelope
alt installer lane budget covers the COMM\n(balance at <latex>R_0</latex> minus earlier group holds)
  Family -> Node : feasible assignment
  Node -[$ca_debit]-> InstallerPurse : debit the installer-region COMM
  Node -[$ca_debit]-> GatewayPurse : debit the gateway's own work and fee
  Node -> Gateway : receipt (one row per debited purse)
else installer lane budget exhausted
  Reducer -> Reducer : the interaction does not fire\n(failure matrix: missing local capability)
  note right of Reducer $ca_note_amber
    No charge for an unfired
    communication. P1 Rule 4
    token gating.
  end note
end

note over InstallerPurse $ca_note_grey
  Genesis continuations carry the Unit
  signature, which maps to no purse,
  so blessed system signers are never charged.
end note

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| signing clients |
  |<$ca_gate>| proposer, validators, and funding selection |
  |<$ca_process>| reducer and native meter |
  |<$ca_pool>| installer's located purse (wallet keying, DR-28) |
  |<$ca_capability>| gateway's signed sources |
  |<$ca_debit>| debit at settlement |
  |<$ca_instantiate>| funding eligibility and authorization |
endlegend

@enduml
